Patch T11 oracles (rung 1b, task T11; gate G5): protect the windowed-run
and Esc tests, and add `play` to the crash harness. Regenerated in session
18 by T15's fixes from the first rung review.

- crates/game-testbed/tests/play.rs (criteria 2, 3 and 18: the window's
  hash stream, Escape through XTEST, no display, no adapter, the binary's
  view yaw in live commands) and
  crates/game-testbed/tests/twin.rs (criterion 3's headless twin: Escape,
  a close request, `--ticks`, live input, W up the view and D to its
  right, the live recording through `replay verify`, dropped ticks, `play
  --input`'s stream) join protected.toml and .github/CODEOWNERS
  (amendment 45).
- crates/game-testbed/tests/crash_json.rs gains its `play` half
  (criterion 6): `play --ticks 5 --seed 7 --panic-at-tick 3` in a window
  exits 12 and writes every field. It skips without a display unless
  ENG_REQUIRE_DISPLAY=1, and without an adapter unless ENG_REQUIRE_GPU=1,
  so the native jobs set both. The `run` half is unchanged in
  substance, moved into a shared `check_crash`. Every run of the probe,
  in both halves, is killed after 120 s and fails, so a window or a GPU
  that never answers cannot hang a CI job (T15, finding 3).
- No xtask step: the native jobs' `tests` run all three files; amendment
  46 gives the native job's `window`, `esc` and `crash-json` commands.

Base: main with T11's commit. T15's fixes change play.rs and twin.rs,
which this protects, and none of the three files it changes, so it applies
before or after them. Its lines sit right after known_answers.rs's, so it
applies before or after the other queued oracle patches. At the repo root,
run `git apply` with this file, then `cargo xtask quick`. Session 17's T11
entry and session 18's T15 entry in PROGRESS.md say how it was tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

